 ## Investigation dependencies
 
-Architectural discovery informs scoped planning, and scoped evidence can reveal an
-architectural assumption worth revisiting. Neither investigation must universally
-finish before the other starts. Begin useful scoped work once confirmed intent
-and source context support it; expose that ready workload alongside independent
-architectural tasks in the same host boundary.
-
-Use concrete, grounded discoveries to add or redirect only affected work. Track
-which evidence delta has been consumed so replay does not create duplicate tasks
-or restart every broad review. An unresolved architectural question holds only
-work whose interpretation actually depends on its answer, not every inspection of
-those files. A temporarily held frontier is not a completed investigation.
-
-Preserve unchanged issued bindings and accepted results when adding work. Source
-or premise changes still invalidate affected results. Only the full fold consumes
-host submissions; the deterministic plan draw does not. Charter source readers
-remain blind to peer and scoped-review results, even when those tasks are issued
-alongside them. Reconcile required architecture work and targeted follow-ups before
-synthesis can present complete conclusions.
+Architectural preparation finishes before fine-grained inspection begins. This
+is a deliberate phase boundary: required charter, contract/conceptual review,
+clarification and systemic work establish the premises the fine plan relies on.
+Independent preparation lanes may run concurrently, but none bypasses the join.
+Charter source readers remain blind to peer results and retain channel-pure
+packets, comparison/fidelity independence and evidence-grounding checks.
+
+The join pins source identity, confirmed intent and scope, structural facts,
+accepted analyzer inputs and selected broad-review outputs. It commits the basis
+and initial plan together. Later discoveries add findings or bounded follow-up
+tasks over the same source; they do not redirect issued work, mutate its question
+or reopen preparation. A graph error is a finding, not permission to rebuild the
+graph underneath other workers. Unusable premises stop with an honest limitation
+or require an explicit new run.
+
+Required-scope completion derives from accepted evidence. Partial inspection may
+create a canonical remainder dependent on its parent; replay creates neither a
+second remainder nor duplicate discovery work. Selective coverage remains
+selective. Only the full draw consumes host submissions; the deterministic-only
+plan draw neither consumes them nor issues host claims.
 
 ---
 
