+A full draw drains ready deterministic work within a charged-execution budget.
+It may consume landed, bound submissions through shared acceptance, then continue
+from accepted evidence. It returns at a host-input boundary rather than executing
+semantic work itself. Issuing host tasks returns their complete assignments.
+An invocation may also stop because the budget is exhausted, no task can advance,
+operator control is paused or cancelled, or the run is complete.
+
+The deterministic-only draw neither consumes host submissions nor issues host
+claims. It stops at the first boundary requiring host work, even if a host result
+already exists on disk. Budget exhaustion is a structured resumable stop, never
+a reason to discard state or claim completion.
+
+The shared result reports checkpoint state, issued tasks, charged executions
+and a stop reason (`host`, `budget`, `blocked`, `paused`, `cancelled`, `complete`).
+Domain adapters render this as the conversation step. There is no requirement
+that one invocation perform exactly one task or refresh every artifact.
+
+## Safe continuation
+
+Source identity, the sealed basis, task specifications and accepted evidence are
+immutable. Each issued attempt resolves task-output inputs to content-addressed
+references and binds the exact result path and prompt. Resume preserves those
+identities; it does not reconstruct accepted meaning from display artifacts.
+
+The coordinator commits immutable payloads before checkpoint replacement. A crash
+before replacement leaves unreferenced files, not accepted work. A crash after
+replacement leaves accepted work whose identical replay is a no-op. Conflicting
+replay or a superseded attempt cannot advance the run.
+
+A failure must retain accepted evidence, identify the blocking condition and
+avoid claiming progress that did not commit. Unsupported state or damaged
+referenced evidence is preserved for diagnosis rather than automatically reset.
+An uncertain external write must be reconciled before retry, not repeated merely
+because an acceptance response was lost.
+
+## Completion
+
+Only required-scope completion established from accepted evidence can release
+dependent tasks or close a phase. The preparation join must seal the basis and
+initial fine plan before dependent inspection. Finalization produces the machine
+report and its human render without silently dropping required unresolved work.
+A partial report is not a complete audit.
